/-!
# Tight footprints of the joint approaches of the tokens and their stations

Research note `N-22`. The certificates `stTokWNZ`, `stTokWZ` (`Gen/DecWindow`) bound the joint
approach of a token and its station by one box, which comes within distance `2` of the previous
station. Here the approach is split (the rows are generated by the certificate tactics, untrusted;
every step is checked): while the token is still `≥ 3` from the station, the station idles in its
pieces' boxes and the token flies in its glider box (`Reaction.par`); the rest of the approach is
certified (`life_reaction`) in a box that keeps away from the previous station:

* `dsepA_winN_foot`: the approach at station `j` of the line NZ (station frame) stays in
  `Box 362 467 846 919 ∪ Box 372 467 820 919`;
* `dsepA_winZ_foot`: the approach at station `j` of the line Z stays in
  `Box 880 979 (-380) (-286) ∪ Box 940 950 (-290) (-279)`.
-/

set_option linter.style.longLine false

